  "question": {
    "text": "Minimum number of times a fair coin must be tossed so that the probability of getting at least one <strong>head </strong>is more than <math><mn>99</mn><mi>%</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let coin is tossed <math><mi>n</mi></math> times.</p><p>The probability of getting a head in a single throw of a die is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>By using binomial theorem, we know that the probability that an event&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;appear&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;times in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;trials is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo></math>at least are head<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo></math>no head<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup></math></p><p>Using, the given condition, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0.99</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.99</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>As,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence, the minimum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
